Simple Web Stack - www.foobar.com

User access flow:
A user opens a browser and types: www.foobar.com.
The browser asks DNS to resolve the domain name.
The domain foobar.com has a www DNS record pointing to the server IP address 8.8.8.8.
The request is then sent through the Internet to the server at 8.8.8.8 using HTTP or HTTPS.
The Nginx web server receives the request.
Nginx forwards dynamic requests to the application server.
The application server runs the website code from the application files.
If data is needed, the application server queries the MySQL database.
The response goes back from the application server to Nginx, then from Nginx to the user's browser.

